They are the shared conformance set for every implementation that speaks
zkp_req - the Rust matcher, the Kotlin and Swift SDKs, and this verifier.
Vendored rather than fetched so the test suite does not depend on the network,
and the digest is pinned in the test that loads them.

Re-vendor rather than edit. A local change turns a cross-implementation check
into a self-consistency one that passes while the implementations disagree -
which is the single failure this file exists to prevent.
